From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 the toolbar colour sample no longer re-lays out the page

Every scroll that paused for half a second made the next one flicker: the
page vanished for 4 to 7 frames (window background, then white) about
100 ms into the next scroll and came back shifted sideways by up to a
scrollbar's width. ReArcTabCaptureSnapshot scope 2 (tab/071, the top 4 CSS
px for the host's toolbar colour, sampled 250 ms after a scroll settles)
was a clipped Page.captureScreenshot, and DevTools renders a clipped shot
under device emulation (viewport offset and scale), so the renderer laid
the page out again for that frame. Chrome never samples, which is why it
never flickered under the same input.

Scope 2 now copies the top 4 DIP of the view's own surface
(RenderWidgetHostView::CopyFromSurface, no DevTools, no emulation) and
encodes that strip as PNG; the result hops back to the UI sequence and keeps
the epoch and document checks. Scopes 0 and 1 are unchanged. Measured with
synthetic wheel and trackpad scrolling on Wikipedia and a plain page: 29 to
31 blank frames per 8 s before, 0 after, no horizontal shifts; a page with
a red sticky header and no theme-color still turns the toolbar red.

Bridge 0.74.0. Nothing in the C ABI changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-16 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.100 (overlay f66d00b59a).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

